$\begin{align}
x^3\cdot x^4&=x^{3+4}
\\\\
&=x ^7
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $x^m\cdot x^n=x^{m+n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
x^3\cdot x^4&=\underbrace{x\cdot x\cdot x}_\text{3 times}\cdot\underbrace{x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x}_\text{4 times}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x}_\text{7 times}
\\\\
&=x^7
\end{align}$
